  "icd_codes": [
    "C25"
  ],
  "summary": "From a referral with suspected pancreatic cancer to a staged, resectability-classified PDAC presented at the MDT. Ends where the treatment pathway starts. DRAFT for clinicians: requirement levels follow the binding ČOS text; order and resectability definitions come from structure sources; sla_days are local placeholders.",
  "notes": [
    "Tissue is required before chemotherapy (all non-resectable branches and neoadjuvant/induction treatment), with the ČOS/ESMO waiver after two non-diagnostic biopsies. Before upfront surgery it is only recommended (structure source).",
    "The ČOS chapter defines resectability by the tumour's relation to vessels plus CA 19-9 and the patient's condition, but gives no thresholds; NCCN/IAP definitions fill that in as structure.",
    "Supportive care (biliary drainage, pain, nutrition) is required by ČOS for all patients but does not block the MDT.",
    "sla_days are local placeholders, not taken from any source."
  ],
  "vocabulary_additions": {
    "exam_type": [
      "ercp",
      "laparoscopy",
      "genetic_consult",
      "molecular_panel",
      "nutrition_consult"
    ],
    "requirement_kind": [
      "measurement"
    ],
    "requirement_fields": [
      "region (exam: anatomical regions that must be covered)",
      "protocol (exam: e.g. pancreatic multiphase)",
      "any (exam_type list: one of them is enough)"
    ]
  },
